<article class="env-lemma" id="0DIN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DIN">Lemma <span data-tag="0DIN">77.13.4</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0DIK" data-tag="0DIK">77.13.1</a> let $K$ be as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0DIL" data-tag="0DIL">77.13.2</a>. Then $K$ is pseudo-coherent on $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combinging Lemma <a href="/tag/0DIM" data-tag="0DIM">77.13.3</a> and Derived Categories of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CWH" data-tag="0CWH">75.25.7</a> we see that $R\Gamma (X, K \otimes ^\mathbf {L} E)$ is pseudo-coherent in $D(A)$ for all pseudo-coherent $E$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Thus it follows from More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CTT" data-tag="0CTT">76.51.4</a> that $K$ is pseudo-coherent relative to $A$. Since $X$ is of flat and of finite presentation over $A$, this is the same as being pseudo-coherent on $X$, see More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DII" data-tag="0DII">76.45.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>